{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>And you shall say.</b> The tav is second person masculine addressed to Israel, who are the ones returning to their land." "<b>For You were angry with me.</b> Even though You were angry with me, like \"Heal my soul, for I have sinned against You\" (Psalms 41:5)."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 12, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:53:28.209070878Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}